# BB→Jugglebot reload: Ball Butler aims at Jugglebot's ACTIVE catch point (the hand-cup
# plane) and throws; Jugglebot catches it. Orchestrated by the RELOAD action
# (reload_coordinator_node), which OWNS the platform + hand for its duration. Every
# Jugglebot-side arming step precedes the throw (2026-07-23 ordering — BB's firmware
# countdown has no abort opcode): it primes the hand to top the moment preconditions
# pass (CHECKING), RAISES the trajectory/arm_catch latch and confirms it (PREPARING),
# and only then sends the throw (AIMING); the existing catch path (catch_coordinator →
# catch/dynamic_target → trajectory_node build_catch) tilt-aligns + seats the ball, then
# it re-centers; on abort it retracts the hand and re-centers. It runs within the operator's
# ACTIVE streaming mode (TRAJECTORY) and does NOT switch modes — leaving that mode
# mid-sequence is the documented abort (there is no persistent CATCH mode). Preconditions
# are checked before any ball flies (see reload_sequencer.py).
# See the reload-action-catch-latch plan (archived 2026-08-01 under plans/archived/).

float64 throw_delay_s          # delay from now to release; 0 => default 3.0 s
                               # (>= BB's ~2.5 s lead floor — a shorter lead comes back
                               #  REJECTED_BB / CANT_MAKE_LEAD)
float64 catch_vel_scale        # operator catch-speed knob; 0 => config default
                               # JB_OP_CATCH_VEL_SCALE_DEFAULT (0.8, locked in from the
                               # 2026-07-23 third sitting — 1.0 bounced balls out). Scales
                               # the event velocity the hand catch is armed with (effective
                               # hand/ball speed ratio = firmware CATCH_VEL_RATIO 0.6 ×
                               # this). Clamped to [0.3, 1.5] — below, the Teensy windup
                               # budget silently drops the stroke; above, the 7 m/s
                               # event-velocity ceiling binds. Published on
                               # catch/vel_scale at PREPARE; resets to the config default
                               # on disarm.
---
bool success                   # True iff the ball was CAUGHT
string outcome                 # CAUGHT | REJECTED_<code> | ABORTED_<code> | MISSED | MISSED_<code>
                               # MVP CAUGHT evidence is tracker-id-correlated: only the
                               # tracker-assigned id of OUR announced ball counts (a stray
                               # caught ball is ignored). Hand-telemetry rest cross-check
                               # is deferred (implement if 7c shows false CAUGHTs).
float64 catch_error_mm         # tracker last-KF horizontal miss from the catch point — an
                               # in-flight estimate, NOT a settled rest position (NaN if
                               # unknown)
---
string phase                   # CHECKING | PREPARING | AIMING | THROW_PENDING | BALL_IN_FLIGHT | CATCHING | SETTLING
